# Hardware & Spray Control

## GPIO

- Nozzle valve + active pump: GPIO outputs (exact pins in `config/hardware.yaml`).
- Tank level: 2 digital GPIO inputs — `tank_full`, `tank_empty`.
- Do not spray if `tank_empty` active or `tank_full` logic indicates fault.

## Defaults (all configurable in config/UI)

| Parameter | Default | Unit |
|-----------|---------|------|
| `camera_to_nozzle_mm` | 20 | mm |
| `mower_speed_mm_s` | 100 | mm/s (0.1 m/s) |
| `spray_delay_ms` | user-set | ms (added to travel time) |
| `spray_duration_ms` | user-set | ms |
| `camera_fps` | 30 | fps |

## Timing

```python
travel_ms = (camera_to_nozzle_mm / mower_speed_mm_s) * 1000.0
fire_at_ms = detection_timestamp_ms + spray_delay_ms + travel_ms
```

Schedule GPIO fire at `fire_at_ms`; duration = `spray_duration_ms`. Use monotonic clock, not wall clock.

## Power

- Pi + pump on dedicated battery (not mower battery). Document wiring in `docs/hardware.md` when added.
